GT patch 0050: a host loop that dispatches guest code itself (gt::call_guest, used by decompiled code) gets what the
dispatcher has: dispatch_function_at() finds the generated unit that holds a pc (a thread that blocked inside a call
resumes at its return address, in the middle of a function, which only the unit knows), and dispatch_boundary() runs the
scheduler boundary after a dispatch (virtual time, preemption, the wall-clock limit).

